# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local development needs nothing: without DATABASE_URL the app uses an embedded
# Postgres (PGlite) stored in ./.data/pglite.
#
# Production: set DATABASE_URL in Vercel (Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables). Use Supabase's *Transaction pooler* string (Connect → Connection
# string → Transaction pooler, port 6543), with your database password filled in
# (URL-encode it if it contains characters like @ : / # ?).
#
# To run migrations against production from your laptop, put the same line in
# .env.production.local (gitignored) and run `npm run db:migrate:prod`.
# Don't put it in .env.local — `npm run dev` would then use the real database.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# ── Signups ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. If set, new accounts need this code — unless they arrive through a
# group invite link. Keeps strangers out of a public deployment.
# SIGNUP_CODE=pick-something
